@startuml State Pattern - Commission Dispute Resolution

' Define the styles (matching observer pattern style)
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title State Pattern - Commission Dispute Resolution

' State Pattern Structure
interface DisputeState <<State>> {
  +addComment(context, comment, author): void
  +assignReviewer(context, reviewerName): void
  +approve(context, adjustedAmount): void
  +reject(context, reason): void
  +escalate(context, reason): void
  +close(context): void
  +getStateName(): String
  +getAvailableActions(): String
}

' Concrete States
class SubmittedState <<ConcreteState>> {
  +addComment(context, comment, author): void
  +assignReviewer(context, reviewerName): void
  +approve(context, adjustedAmount): void
  +reject(context, reason): void
  +escalate(context, reason): void
  +close(context): void
  +getStateName(): String
  +getAvailableActions(): String
}

class UnderReviewState <<ConcreteState>> {
  +addComment(context, comment, author): void
  +assignReviewer(context, reviewerName): void
  +approve(context, adjustedAmount): void
  +reject(context, reason): void
  +escalate(context, reason): void
  +close(context): void
  +getStateName(): String
  +getAvailableActions(): String
}

class EscalatedState <<ConcreteState>> {
  +addComment(context, comment, author): void
  +assignReviewer(context, reviewerName): void
  +approve(context, adjustedAmount): void
  +reject(context, reason): void
  +escalate(context, reason): void
  +close(context): void
  +getStateName(): String
  +getAvailableActions(): String
}

class ResolvedState <<ConcreteState>> {
  +addComment(context, comment, author): void
  +assignReviewer(context, reviewerName): void
  +approve(context, adjustedAmount): void
  +reject(context, reason): void
  +escalate(context, reason): void
  +close(context): void
  +getStateName(): String
  +getAvailableActions(): String
}

class ClosedState <<ConcreteState>> {
  +addComment(context, comment, author): void
  +assignReviewer(context, reviewerName): void
  +approve(context, adjustedAmount): void
  +reject(context, reason): void
  +escalate(context, reason): void
  +close(context): void
  +getStateName(): String
  +getAvailableActions(): String
}

' Context
class DisputeContext <<Context>> {
  -currentState: DisputeState
  -disputeId: String
  -submittedBy: String
  -originalAmount: BigDecimal
  -adjustedAmount: BigDecimal
  -reviewer: String
  -commentHistory: List<String>
  -submittedDate: LocalDateTime
  +setState(newState: DisputeState): void
  +addComment(comment, author): void
  +assignReviewer(reviewerName): void
  +approve(adjustedAmount): void
  +reject(reason): void
  +escalate(reason): void
  +close(): void
  +getStateName(): String
  +getAvailableActions(): String
  +displayStatus(): void
  +displayHistory(): void
}

' Relationships
DisputeState <|.. SubmittedState
DisputeState <|.. UnderReviewState
DisputeState <|.. EscalatedState
DisputeState <|.. ResolvedState
DisputeState <|.. ClosedState

DisputeContext o--> "1" DisputeState : currentState

DisputeContext ..> DisputeState : delegates to >
DisputeState ..> DisputeContext : manages >

' State transitions (showing some key transitions)
SubmittedState .right.> UnderReviewState : assignReviewer()
SubmittedState ..> EscalatedState : escalate()
UnderReviewState ..> ResolvedState : approve()/reject()
UnderReviewState ..> EscalatedState : escalate()
EscalatedState .left.> UnderReviewState : assignReviewer()
EscalatedState ..> ResolvedState : approve()/reject()
ResolvedState ..> ClosedState : close()
ResolvedState ..> EscalatedState : escalate()

' Pattern component notes
note right of DisputeState
  <b>State Interface</b>
  Defines contract for all states.
  Each method represents an action
  that can be performed on a dispute.
  States decide which actions are valid.
end note

note bottom of SubmittedState
  <b>Initial State</b>
  - Can add comments
  - Can assign reviewer → transitions to UNDER_REVIEW
  - Can escalate → transitions to ESCALATED
  - Cannot approve/reject (no reviewer yet)
  - Cannot close (not resolved yet)
end note

note bottom of UnderReviewState
  <b>Active Review State</b>
  - Can add review comments
  - Can reassign reviewer
  - Can approve → transitions to RESOLVED
  - Can reject → transitions to RESOLVED
  - Can escalate → transitions to ESCALATED
end note

note bottom of EscalatedState
  <b>Management Review State</b>
  - Requires higher authority
  - Can approve with override → transitions to RESOLVED
  - Can reject → transitions to RESOLVED
  - Can reassign → transitions to UNDER_REVIEW
  - Already at highest level (no further escalation)
end note

note bottom of ResolvedState
  <b>Decision Made State</b>
  - Decision has been made (approved/rejected)
  - Can add comments (read-mostly)
  - Can close → transitions to CLOSED
  - Can re-escalate if disagreeing → ESCALATED
  - Cannot change decision directly
end note

note bottom of ClosedState
  <b>Terminal State</b>
  - No modifications allowed
  - Read-only access
  - Final state in lifecycle
  - Cannot transition to any other state
end note

note left of DisputeContext
  <b>Context</b>
  Maintains reference to current state
  and delegates all requests to it.
  Doesn't know which concrete state
  it has - only the State interface.

  <b>Key Method:</b>
  setState() allows states to
  transition to other states.
end note

' Legend
legend right
  <b>State Pattern Components:</b>

  <b>State (Interface):</b> Defines interface for
  encapsulating state-specific behavior.

  <b>ConcreteState:</b> Implements behavior
  associated with a particular state.
  Knows which state(s) can follow it.

  <b>Context:</b> Maintains current state
  and delegates requests to state object.
  Provides interface for clients.

  <b>Key Benefits:</b>
  • Eliminates complex if/else chains
  • Makes state transitions explicit
  • Easy to add new states
  • Each state is independently testable
  • Follows Open/Closed Principle
endlegend

@enduml